    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nWould it be possible to add an optional parameter to `MiniPick.builtin.resume` so that it executes the query again?\n\nLet me explain, if I'm refactoring some code I could do a search for a particular word that should be replaced/modified, then I start replacing every occurrence and run `MiniPick.builtin.resume` to check what is missing. With the current implementation the pick results are static so even if the match does not exist anymore its shown in the picker.\n\nOf course, it's ok if this doesn't fit the purpose of that picker.\nLove your work btw.",
