        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nYeah, I am afraid this is a bit contradicting the purpose of actually \"resuming\": it brings up the picker in exactly the same state as it was left. Re-running the query is a different picker with possibly different array of items.\n\nIf you run `grep` picker (and not `grep_live`) frequently, then it should be feasible to write thin custom wrappers that would get the word from the input in one mapping and use the latest such word in another mapping.\n\nTwo things that I find myself doing in this kind of situations are 1) send result to the quickfix list (mark some or all items and press `<M-CR>`) and work with it; or 2) delete single character and re-enter it if resumed picker is from `grep_live`.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
